Description: Downloads simulated Census tract maps and plans for every U.S.
    county across the 2000, 2010, and 2020 decennial Censuses from the Harvard
    Dataverse. This data supports the study of the Modifiable Areal Unit Problem
    by allowing researchers to quantify how sensitive any tract-level
    statistic is to the choice of geographic boundaries. Builds on data from
    Brown, Kenny, and Simko (2025) <doi:10.31235/osf.io/nv5up_v2>.
